  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd `examples/catalog/probing/probe-face` with an original block, generator, script, project, NC program, metadata, and README.\nProbe1 touches the stock top at Z13. Face1 then cuts the stock to Z12.\nThe project embeds the mesh. The generated guide lists link to the case under Probe and Face.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe catalog had no case that showed a Probe operation before a Face operation.\nThe case follows `examples/catalog/README.md` and the requirements in #2874.\nThe decision is in `docs/decisions/2874-probe-face.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `catalog_probing_probe_face::probes_before_first_cut` failed before the case existed. It passes with the case.\n- `catalog_probing_probe_face::regenerates` passes.\n- `catalog_probing_probe_face::rebuilds` passes.\n- Remove the case to restore the upstream state: the pin fails. Restore the case: the pin passes.\n- Remove the G31 lines: the pin fails. Restore the lines: the pin passes.\n- No production guard changed. The new case has no upstream file to restore with `git show`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes on the final tree.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog` passes: 37 passed, 4 ignored.\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check` passes for all 14 cases.\n\nThe gate test-name lookup could not find the included pin. The equivalent direct Cargo test ran the red and green pin checks.\nThe first quick gate became void when documentation changed during the run. The next run passed with the tree unchanged.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nAdd one NC golden: `examples/catalog/probing/probe-face/probe-face.nc` (82 lines).\nThe program has G31 touches, contact checks, and a G54 update before Face1 cuts at Z12.\nI read the full NC diff. Each line belongs to the new two-operation case.\nNo existing NC or CL golden changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical machine run, measured stock offset, other probe modes, or GUI run.\nThe heavy dry-run reaches `app heavy: example_catalog`. Its release-only ignored tests were not run.\nThe PR stays a draft.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #3103 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nIt changes the Bore section of `site/content/guide/operations/operations-2d.md`.\nThis PR adds one generated link in the Face section. The changed lines do not overlap.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: Add a catalog example that probes the stock top before facing a block.\n\nFixes #2874\n",
